          id: 'building-ai-agents-03-predict-output-1',
          kind: 'predict-output',
          title: 'What does a loop with a limit print?',
          story: 'A scripted stand-in for a model: it returns prepared decisions and calls no real model. The loop is the one from the lesson, in JavaScript.',
          prompt: 'The script asks for the same lookup three times and only finishes on its fourth decision. The limit is three steps. Work out what the program prints.',
          concept: 'a step limit stops the loop',
          language: 'javascript',
